            "body": "AI findings below. Please do NOT rebase when pushing a fix.\r\n\r\n1. **`:uptime` mistranslated** (L7006): \"Up %s\" is translated as \"Yuxarı %s\", which means \"upward\", not \"running for\". Something like \"İş vaxtı: %s\" would fit.\r\n\r\n2. **Swap-file (E325) dialog hotkeys** (L3783, L3786):\r\n   - Quit's hotkey is the non-ASCII `ç` (\"&Çıx\"), which can't be typed on a US keyboard layout.\r\n   - `r` now selects \"Edit anyway\" instead of Recover. A user who presses `r` out of habit to recover gets \"Edit anyway\" and may then save over the file without the recovered changes.\r\n   - `tr.po` avoids both problems with ASCII hotkeys (\"Çı&k\", \"Kur&tar\").\r\n\r\n3. **`#, c-format` flags are on the wrong entries** (from L52 on): 240 entries that contain `%` items lack the flag, and 247 entries without `%` items have it (e.g. `--Deleted--` at L37). `msgfmt -c` skips format checking on the\r\nunflagged entries.\r\n   - The file is also not in msgmerge's normal layout: 211 lines are longer than 80 columns, and strings aren't split at `\\n`. Running `msgmerge` changes about 1,700 lines.\r\n\r\n4. **Doubled punctuation:**\r\n   - \"Argument missing after\" (L3201) ends with `:`, but `print_mainerr` (main.c) already appends `: \"%s\"`, so `nvim -u` prints `...yoxdur:: \"-u\"`.\r\n   - \"Backwards range given, OK to swap\" (L2478) ends with `?`, but `ask_yesno` already appends ` (y/n)?`, so the prompt ends with `? (y/n)?`.\r\n\r\n5. **Typos** (L5919, L5971): \"cTRL-U\" and \"cTRL-F\" in the `'scroll'`/`'window'` option descriptions.\r\n\r\n6. **\"string\" and \"line\" are the same word (`sətir`)** (L3896): E348 \"No string under cursor\" reads as \"no line under cursor\", and E928/E1174 (\"Sətir tələb olunur\") read as \"line required\".\r\n\r\n7. **Inconsistent type names** (e.g. L923):\r\n   - Blob: \"ikilik məlumat bloku\", \"bayt bloku\", \"ikili verilənlər bloku\".\r\n   - Float: \"sürüşən nöqtəli\", \"sürüşən vergüllü\", \"üzən nöqtəli\".\r\n   - Callback: \"geriçağırış\", \"geri çağırış\", \"əks çağırış\".\r\n\r\n8. **`:confirm qa` hotkeys** (L455): in the Yes/No/Save All/Discard All/Cancel dialog, `y` selects \"Save All\" because Yes is `b` (\"Bəli\").\r\n\r\n9. **Column headers vs. fixed widths** (e.g. L5536): translated headers are longer than the fixed-width columns. For example, \"Arqumentlər\" (11 chars) sits over the 5-wide Args column in `:command`. The same happens in `:jumps` (L3398),\r\n`:changes`, `:registers`, `:undolist`, `:syntime` and `:tags`.\r\n\r\n10. **`[noeol]` → `[ssyox]`** (L328): an invented abbreviation that readers won't recognize.\r\n",
